Your choices and rights
You can ask us to:

tell you what personal information we hold about you and give you a copy;
correct information that’s wrong;
delete your conversations before the 90 days are up;
remove the entries for your requests from our service log;
stop using your information for a particular purpose.

Email prompthumanhq@gmail.com from the email address you paid with. That address is how we find your records and confirm they are yours. We’ll reply to it and ask you to confirm before we delete anything, because deletion can’t be undone. If you never paid, or can no longer use the address you paid with, include your conversation ID instead.
Tell us which you want: only your conversations and messages deleted, or your service log entries removed as well. If the address you paid with is shared, for example a company’s accounts mailbox, a request from it covers everyone who paid through it. We can’t delete a conversation while a refund or a payment on it is still being settled; we’ll tell you if that applies and delete it once it is.
We’ll respond within 30 days. We may need to keep payment records the law requires us to keep. The service log holds no names, contact details or request text. Its entries are tied to you only through the client code, so we find them from your paying address, or from a conversation ID, and remove them if you ask.
